# Rich Text Description Formatting Guide

## Overview
You can now add **formatted descriptions** to your tooltip data! This allows you to create visually appealing tooltips with line breaks, bold text, bullet lists, and more.

## How to Use

In your settings file (e.g., `fs25.settings.js`), add a `description` property to your `tooltipData` entries using HTML formatting:

```javascript
tooltipData: {
    "YourFile.zip": {
        images: [
            "image1.jpg",
            "image2.jpg"
        ],
        description: "<b>Your Title</b><br><br>Your description here..."
    }
}
```

## Supported HTML Tags

### Text Formatting
- `<b>` or `<strong>` - **Bold text** (appears in bright white)
- `<i>` or `<em>` - *Italic text* (appears slightly dimmed)

### Line Breaks
- `<br>` - Single line break
- `<br><br>` - Double line break (paragraph spacing)

### Lists
- `<ul>` - Unordered bullet list
- `<ol>` - Ordered numbered list
- `<li>` - List item

### Paragraphs
- `<p>` - Paragraph tags (automatically adds spacing)

### Code
- `<code>` - Inline code formatting

## Examples

### Simple Description with Bold and Line Breaks
```javascript
description: "<b>Map Name</b><br><br>This is a great map with lots of features!"
```

### Description with Bullet Points
```javascript
description: "<b>Huron County</b> features:<br><br>• Large fields<br>• Realistic terrain<br>• North American setting<br>• 16x map size"
```

### Description with HTML List
```javascript
description: "<b>Features:</b><ul><li>Large fields for crops</li><li>Realistic terrain</li><li>Multiple farmyards</li></ul>"
```

### Description with Bold and Italic
```javascript
description: "<b>Back Roads County</b><br><br>Experience <i>authentic American farming</i> with:<br>• Winding roads<br>• Mixed farming<br>• 4x terrain"
```

### Multiple Formatting Styles Combined
```javascript
description: "<b>Judith Plains, Montana</b><br><br>Experience the <i>wide-open spaces</i> of Montana with:<br>• Vast plains<br>• Mountain views<br>• <b>4x</b> map size"
```

## Tips

1. **Use `<br><br>` for spacing** - Double line breaks create nice paragraph spacing
2. **Bold important text** - Use `<b>` tags for map names, feature titles, etc.
3. **Use bullet points** - Either with `<br>•` or with `<ul><li>` tags
4. **Keep it concise** - Tooltips should be informative but not overwhelming
5. **Test your formatting** - Hover over items to see how the tooltip looks

## Quick Reference

| What You Want | HTML Code | Example |
|---------------|-----------|---------|
| Bold text | `<b>text</b>` | `<b>Important</b>` |
| Italic text | `<i>text</i>` | `<i>special</i>` |
| Line break | `<br>` | `Line 1<br>Line 2` |
| Bullet point | `<br>•` | `<br>• Item 1<br>• Item 2` |
| List | `<ul><li>item</li></ul>` | `<ul><li>One</li><li>Two</li></ul>` |

## Example Entry from fs25.settings.js

```javascript
"Huron County 16X.zip": {
    images: [
        "https://example.com/image1.jpg",
        "https://example.com/image2.jpg",
        "https://example.com/image3.jpg",
    ],
    description: "<b>Huron County</b> is a massive 16x map featuring:<br><br>• Expansive North American farmland<br>• Multiple large fields for crop cultivation<br>• Realistic terrain and landscape<br>• Perfect for large-scale farming operations"
}
```

## Notes

- All HTML is sanitized for safety
- Descriptions support both inline styles and structured HTML
- The styling is already configured in the CSS - just use the HTML tags!
- You can mix and match different formatting styles as needed